[issue.1754]
number = 1754
title = "[Coherence] Task 22.31.564 tells the Rust runtime to add a replay fuel total to the replay record, but the kernel parses that record at fixed offsets and is not in the task's paths"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "already-fixed"
evidence = "Commit bffd004c702409ced99e8118034947b18e5a42b1 implemented replay fuel as a derived total of existing committed boundary fields, recomputed and checked at programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/replay_record.rs:449 and reconstructed by portable decoding at programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/portable_replay.rs:732 without an extra serialized total (programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_call.rs:1360); the current encoder writes version 2 at programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/replay_record.rs:533 and the kernel accepts that version and its length-prefixed header while preserving the exact witness-length check at src/modules/programs/call.c:3271 and src/modules/programs/call.c:3298, with the native staged layout unchanged at src/modules/programs/state_record.c:566, fuel recomputation and CPU parity assertions at programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/tests/repair_22_31_564.rs:114 and programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/tests/repair_22_31_564.rs:131, and native version-2 CALL acceptance assertions at tests/programs/test_ai_host_boundary.c:678."
close_comment = "Replay fuel is reconstructed from the committed per-boundary fuel values, so recording the total adds no field to the serialized replay record. The runtime and kernel agree on the current version-2 record format, with tests covering recomputation, unchanged guest CPU usage and native record acceptance."
